Package: R2GUESS
Title: Bayesian Variable Selection for Multiple Correlated Outcomes using GUESS
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-11-12
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Leonardo",
           family = "Bottolo",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "lb664@cam.ac.uk")
Description: R interface to GUESS, a C++ implementation of Evolutionary
    Stochastic Search (ESS) for sparse Bayesian variable selection in linear
    regression with one or several correlated outcomes (e.g. multi-tissue gene
    expression) and many predictors (e.g. SNPs). Provides functions to run
    GUESS with parallel chains, resume and extend runs, check convergence,
    summarise marginal posterior probabilities of inclusion and best models,
    and assess significance by permutation-based false discovery rate. The
    computationally intensive linear algebra can optionally be offloaded to a
    GPU through the CULA library; the default CPU build requires only the GNU
    Scientific Library.
